> It depends what is the distribution of the function rnz()[1].
> 
> If we know that then it's easy. Barring no other prayer time-out 
> affecting actions than prayer (not praying on cross-aligned altar) then:
> 
> If non-crowned and not have killed the wizard or performed the 
> invocation then prayer time-out is increased by rnz(350) when praying.
> 
> If non-crowned but have killed the wizard or performed the invocation or 
> crowned and not have killed wizard or performed the invocation then the 
> prayer time-out is incresed by rnz(350)+rnz(1000) when praying.
> 
> If crowned and killed the wizard or performed the invocation then the 
> prayer time-out is increased by rnz(350)+2*rnz(1000) when praying.
> 
> [1] About the distribution of rnz():
> 
> rnz() defines a new variable tmp which get's assigned in the form a*b 
> where:
> 
> a is a random evenly distributed number in the range 1000..1999 and
> 
> b is a random unenvenly distributed number in the range 1 to 5 or 
> character level / 3 whichever is higher [2].
> 
> Then the return value of rnz(x) is half the time x*tmp/1000 and half the 
> time x*1000/tmp.
> 
> [2] In this particular case the distribution of the values for b follow 
> the pattern:
> 
> value probability
>   1      3/4
>   2      3/16
>   3      3/64
>   4      3/256
> etc.
> 
> Generally for a value n the probability is 3/4^n, remembering that there 
> is upper limit of 5 or chatracter level / 3 so for the highest value n 
> the probability is 1/4^(n-1).
> 
> So go on an pluck those numbers into your spredsheet and give use the 
> definite answer.

